            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Economic Reforms</strong><br>\nUnder Hussein's leadership, Jordan underwent significant economic transformation. He encouraged foreign investment and introduced economic reforms that helped to liberalize the economy. These efforts resulted in a more modern and diversified economy, with growth in sectors such as tourism and information technology.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Family and Personal Life</strong><br>\nKing Hussein was married four times and had eleven children. His family life was often under public scrutiny, but he was known to be a devoted father and husband. His personal interests included amateur radio and aviation, and he was known for his piloting skills.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Legacy</strong><br>\nKing Hussein died of cancer on February 7, 1999. His legacy includes a period of relative stability and modernization in Jordan, despite the region's turmoil. He is remembered for his diplomatic efforts and his role in creating a foundation for peace in the Middle East. His son, King Abdullah II, succeeded him and continues to build on his father's work.</p>\n"
              },
